[h2]Entity Culling[/h2]
Temporarily hides units, vehicles (including static weapons), ammo boxes and weapon holders that terrain or buildings block from the camera. Each client tests visibility from its own camera, so hiding only affects rendering on that client. Hidden entities still simulate and make sound. Entities are revealed when they become visible again, and stopping the addon reveals everything it hid.

[h2]Server settings[/h2]
[list]
[*]Frame budget (1 ms by default): how much time each client can spend on visibility tests per frame.
[*]Minimum distance (10 m): entities this close to the camera or to the player's unit or vehicle are never hidden.
[*]Check interval (0.2 s) and consecutive checks before hiding (3).
[*]Prediction (0.5 s): how much camera and entity movement a check covers.
[*]Debug overlay (off): hidden and checked entities, worker time and FPS on every client.
[/list]

[h2]How to enable it[/h2]
In Eden, place the [b]Entity Culling[/b] module to use it in that scenario. A trigger can turn the module on and off. Enable it without an Eden module through [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=450814997]CBA_A3[/url]. Open [b]Addon Options → Entity Culling[/b], check [b]Enable Entity Culling[/b] and restart the mission. In multiplayer, use the Server tab.

